Project: Low-Cost Infrastructure
Project or Feature Description
Purpose and Scope: This project aims to research, evaluate, and plan the transition of Amazethu's current infrastructure from AWS to a suite of low-cost or free-tier providers. The goal is to sustain operations for the current user base (~30 active users) at near-zero cost until the user count scales significantly (e.g., to thousands), at which point a move back to a robust enterprise cloud like AWS can be justified. The scope covers the evaluation of alternatives for dynamic hosting, containerized compute (Node.js and Python/ML), object storage, and API management. The goal is to identify options that reduce operational costs during the alpha/beta phase while maintaining the current deployment speed and security standards.
Main Objectives and Goals:
Document current state: Catalog all AWS services currently in use and their purposes
Cost Reduction: Research and identify viable free-tier infrastructure providers or a combination of services that reduces monthly infrastructure spend significantly for the current user volume.
Feasibility Analysis and Vendor Evaluation: Create comparison matrix of features, limits, and costs of providers against current AWS usage.
Provide recommendations: Deliver decision framework with clear thresholds
Formulate Migration Roadmap: Create a low-risk plan to transition services while maintaining Squarespace DNS management.
Scopes and Limits:
Will cover:
Research and evaluation of AWS-hosted components: ECS Fargate (be-app, botai), Amplify (fe-web), API Gateway, etc
Comparison of free-tier offerings from alternative providers (Cloudflare, Render, Railway, etc.)
Analysis of migration complexity and effort for each component
Documentation of scaling thresholds and cost projections
Testing approach for validating alternatives (POC on STAG environment)
Recommendations for phased transition plan
Will not cover:
Mobile app (Expo) - remains on current infrastructure as it is not of highest priority
Website - already migrated to Firebase Hosting
MongoDB Atlas [ confirmation if it's free]
PROD environment changes
Key Definitions:
Free-tier provider: Cloud infrastructure provider offering services at zero cost up to defined usage limits
Low-cost provider: Cloud infrastructure provider offering services at significantly reduced cost compared to enterprise providers like AWS
Scaling threshold: Usage level at which free-tier limits are exceeded and paid tiers are triggered
POC (Proof of Concept): Small-scale deployment to validate technical feasibility before full migration
Requirements Definition
Target Personas:
A stakeholder: Product leads, technical advisors, and decision-makers who will use this research to make infrastructure decisions.
Developer: Dev team members responsible for the development and maintenance of  e app.
User Stories:
As a stakeholder, I should be able to:
Review clear comparison of infrastructure options and costs
Understand scaling thresholds and when free tiers become insufficient
Make informed decisions about infrastructure strategy
Approve migration roadmap based on research findings
As a developer, I should be able to:
Replicate our current GitHub Actions deployment workflow on the new provider so that our "push-to-deploy" automation remains intact.
 Access and manage environment variables and secrets (like API keys) through the new provider's interface.
Access real-time deployment logs and historical logs for debugging failed builds or runtime errors.
Monitor resource utilization
Verify the health and state of services. Eg, healthy, deploying, crashed, running etc
  Map our Squarespace custom domains to the new infrastructure without complex DNS re-configurations or long propagation delays.
  Receive automated notifications if a deployment fails or if we are approaching the free-tier usage limits.

